shape: Directional Twin
shape description: Symmetrical shape with slightly shifted stance; versatile for freestyle with added stability of directional design; performs well regular and switch but excels in one direction
camber type: Fusion Camber
camber description: Predominantly positive camber with small zones of rocker in nose and tail; versatile all mountain camber profile that is responsive without being too aggressive
width: Standard, Wide
sidecut type: Tri-Radial Sidecut
sidecut description: Three radii create complete curve; wider radius in nose and tail with tighter radius through middle; prevents over turning, hang ups, and offers more natural turn initiation
mounting pattern: 2x4 Inserts
laminate: Triax Upper Glass, Triax Lower Glass, Twin Single Bamboo Omega HotRods
laminate description: Triaxial fiberglass in three angles above core for torsional rigidity and extra snap; singular Bamboo HotRod in nose and tail for torsional flexibility while staying poppy; HotRod wrapped in additional Carbon sleeve for additional pop and responsiveness
core: Stomp Core
core materials: Poplar
core description: Highly stable and predictable core made entirely of Poplar wood
base: SinterStrong Base
base description: Low maintenance sintered base that is extremely versatile and fast
3D base technology: Directional Diamond 3D
3D base description: Wide flat section in middle, 3D curve tapering past contact points in nose; stable flat riding, easier turns, disperses powder with ease
tail feature: Tail Double Kick
tail feature description: Aggressive two-part rise in tail for more pop, enhanced torsional stability, and smoother landings
terrain: Groomers, fresh snow, changing terrain, all mountain
riding style: All Mountain, Freeride, Carving, Freestyle
one board quiver: Yes (described as dependable one board quiver)
